# Places journal rules

- Index: `public/content/places/index.json` (listing fields only). One story file per visit: `public/content/places/<slug>.txt`. One photo under `public/assets/places/`.
- Index fields: slug, name, region, country, visitedOn, type (`trek`|`travel`), summary, photo, photoCredit, optional `instagramUrl`.
- The `.txt` file is the trail story. Separate paragraphs with a blank line. Do not put the long story back into the index.
- Optional `instagramUrl` (post/reel share link) replaces the photo on the detail page with a compact Instagram Reel thumbnail card (opens Instagram in a new tab on click).
- Notes should cover how you reach the place and how the trek/day went (user may edit later).
- Prefer the user’s real visits; do not reintroduce dummy demo places.
- No end-user “edit this JSON” instructional copy in the UI.
- Photo credits may note placeholders until personal trail photos replace them.
